The attached image (Figure 5) illustrates that Nano-11 enhances the transport of antigens to lymph nodes. Flow cytometry data (A) shows that Nano-11, when co-administered with ovalbumin (OVA), leads to a higher mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) of OVA in OVA-containing cells in the draining lymph nodes at both Day 1 and Day 2 compared to soluble OVA or OVA with aluminum hydroxide (AH). This is further quantified in plot B, demonstrating Nano-11's superior ability to deliver antigen to APCs on a per-cell basis. Plot C highlights that Nano-11 significantly increases the percentage of migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) among OVA-positive cells, indicating effective targeting to key antigen-presenting cells.